indent>\n\n<b>Remote App (& Remote Web App)</b><indent=60px>\n- Links & hierarchies: Category link buttons now switch within the remote app instead of the server, enabling hierarchical navigation remotely.\n- Hidden categories: Hidden categories are now also hidden on the remote app and web.\nUpdate the remote app by downloading it to benefit from those changes.</indent>\n\n<b>Instructions</b><indent=60px>\n- Dynamic actions: For each instruction item, choose which actions to run.\n- Action sources: Use the actions configured for left/right/middle click, or the action used to launch from the grid.\n- Result: Enables more flexible, context-driven instructions.</indent>\n\n<b>Touch</b><indent=60px>\n- Long-press = right-click: Added where missing (for example, link players and change play mode).\n- Safer editing on mobile: Resize and move panels only in Edit mode to prevent accidental layout changes.\n- Mode switch polish: Fixed layout issues when switching between Phone and Desktop modes.\n- Menus on touch: Menus no longer auto-close immediately on touch displays.</indent>\n\n<b>Recordings & Freesound Files</b><indent=60px>\n- Project-relative storage: With Relative paths projects, recordings and Freesound downloads are stored next to the project file.\n- Configurable folders: Folder names are configurable via Project → Edit.</indent>\n\n<b>MIDI</b><indent=60px>\n- Output selection: New bindings to select the next or previous audio output, or specific outputs by index.\n- Absolute mappings: Bind a MIDI control to a playable or category so it triggers regardless of the current category.\n- Configuration location: Set in the Edit popup.</indent>\n\n<b>Scheduler</b><indent=60px>\n- New Scheduler panel: Open via View → Views → Scheduler.\n- Schedule to clock time: Drag an item to the panel and set a play time.\n- Repeats: Configure repetitions (for example, play “Song 1” at 20:30 and repeat every hour).</indent>\n\n<b>Waveform</b><indent=60px>\n- Persist waveforms: Options → Visual → Waveform now allows saving waveform data next to the audio file.\n- Faster loading: Saved waveforms load near-instantly on next laun</indent>\n\n<b>Bug fixes</b><indent=60px>\n- Fix video loops with custom start/stop times\n- Fix clock time drifting issue\n- Sound Effects User values applied: Fixed an issue where saved effect values (echo, reverb, …) were not applied on activation.</indent></indent>", "link_url": "https://www.soundshow.app/downloads", "link_label": "Download the new version", "image": "", "create_date": "2026-02-04 16:03:53", "message_date": "2026-02-04", "message_type": "update"}, {"id": 18, "title": "Update 14.12.2025 - Mobile Pro Release", "description": "<indent=20px><b>Mobile / Android</b><indent=40px>\n<b>Activate Mobile Pro on Android:</b> \nYou can now activate Sound Show Mobile Pro directly on Android devices.\nMobile Pro is a separate, lower-priced license.\n\n<b>Features summary:</b>\n<indent=60px>Removes limits on number of sounds and tabs\nAdd customization options (grids size, skins, icons...)\nUnlocks the standard desktop touch Sound Show interface on mobile</indent></indent>\n\n<indent=20px><b>Lock Toggle (Safety):</b><indent=40px>\nPrevents unintended actions across Phone View and Desktop View — including input from touch, keyboard, and MIDI controllers.\nPhone View: Toggle is in the navigation bar\nDesktop View: Toggle is in the menu bar.\nIt is hidden by default. Enable via Options → Visuals → Lock button.</indent></indent>\n\n<indent=20px><b>Phone View</b><indent=40px>\n<b>Action Menu for taps/clicks:</b> \nChoose which actions are available when you tap/click in Phone View (Options -> Actions)\n\n<b>Customizable Navigation Bar:</b> \nHide specific navigation buttons to simplify the UI (Options → Visuals → Navigation Bar)</indent></indent>\n", "link_url": "https://www.soundshow.app/downloads", "link_label": "Download the new version", "image": "", "create_date": "2025-12-15 13:02:03", "message_date": "2025-12-15", "message_type": "update"}, {"id": 17, "title": "Latest Updates - 04 Dec and 24 Nov", "description": "<indent=20px><b>Release Notes - 2025-12-04</b><indent=40px>\n<b>Playlists</b><indent=60px>\n<b>Playing indicator:</b> When a playlist is loaded in the Playlist panel with Autoplay enabled, its button shows a playing icon.\n<b>Toggle from the grid:</b> Click a playlist button in the grid to toggle playback (and Toggle Fade if enabled). This also toggles Autoplay for that playlist.\n<b>Crossfade between playlists:</b> Crossfading from the grid will stop Autoplay on the current playlist and start Autoplay on the selected playlist.</indent>\n<b>Tooltip clarity:</b> Corrected and polished tooltips in the Instruction and Playlist panels.\n<b>Faster file access:</b> Reduced latency before audio playback begins.\n<b>Audio engine:</b> Updated engine</indent>\n\n<indent=20px><b>Release Notes - 2025-11-24</b><indent=40px>\n<b>New & Improved</b><indent=60px>\n<b>“Unlock on Click” action:</b> Option to unlock a button by simply clicking it (<i>Options → Main → Unlock when interacting with…</i>).\n<b>Video crossfades:</b> Videos now crossfade with each other without a black frame. Fade-out and fade-in happen simultaneously.\n<b>Quick Edit shortcut:</b> Hold a configurable key to enter Edit mode; release to return to normal. Handy for quick edits (e.g., drag & drop into the Playlist panel). (<i>Options → Keyboard → General → Quick Edit</i>)\n<b>Project-wide normalization:</b> Normalize volume across the entire project via a new button in a category’s edit popup (<i>Normalize all categories</i>). You can also normalize just selected categories.\n<b>MIDI bindings for play modes:</b> Bind MIDI to jump directly to Replace, Toggle, or Toggle Fade modes.\n<b>Mouse action to add to playlist:</b> Assign any mouse button (via the Actions panel) to add a sound to a playlist.\n<b>Player sliders:</b> Improved text height/legibility on position sliders.</indent>\n<b>Fixes</b><indent=60px>\n<b>License activation:</b> Fixed an issue where rich-text tags (underline, bold, etc.) could break activation.\n<b>Smooth loop:</b> Resolved an edge case where smooth looping could unexpectedly stop other sounds.</indent></indent>", "link_url": "https://soundshow.app/downloads", "link_label": "Download the new version", "image": "", "create_date": "2025-12-05 11:15:16", "message_date": "2025-12-04", "message_type": "update"}, {"id": 16, "title": "Update 05.11.2025 - Hierarchical Categories", "description": "<indent=20px><b>Folder Import Improved</b><indent=40px>\n<b>Import modes:</b>\n<indent=60px><b>Single Category (flat):</b> Import all items into one category.\n<b>Single Category with Tags: Import all items into one category; each item is tagged with its subfolder name.\n<b>(Pro) Category Directory: Create a parent category for the top folder and child categories for each subfolder.</indent>\n<b>Category Directory behavior:</b>\n<indent=60px>Parent includes link buttons to child categories; children include a link back to the parent.\nChild categories are hidden from the category grid by default (visible in Edit mode).</indent></indent></indent>\n\n<indent=20px><b>Categories & Navigation</b><indent=40px>\n<b>Category Link Button:</b> Jump directly to a target category with one click.\n<b>Show/Hide Hidden Categories:</b> New toggle in the category grid (available in Edit mode only).\n<b>Back/Forward Navigation:</b> Return to previously selected categories with Back and Forward buttons (keyboard and MIDI bindings supported).\n<b>Bulk Delete:</b> Delete multiple selected categories at once.</indent></indent>\n\n<indent=20px><b>Fixes</b><indent=40px>\n<b>Long-press & Right-click:</b> Resolved an issue where a long-press (to trigger right-click on touch) could erroneously trigger a left-click afterward.\n<b>Playlist deletions:</b> Playlist items now delete correctly.</indent></indent>", "link_url": "https://soundshow.app/downloads", "link_label": "Download the new version", "image": "", "create_date": "2025-11-06 09:16:25", "message_date": "2025-11-06", "message_type": "update"}, {"id": 15, "title": "Update 25.10.2025", "description": "<indent=20px><b>Security</b><indent=40px>\n<b>Engine update:</b> Updated the Unity3D engine to address an important security vulnerability.\n<b>Recommendation:</b> We strongly recommend updating all your Sound Show installations, including Sound Show Remote and Sound Show Mobile.</indent></indent>\n\n<indent=20px><b>Project Saving & Backups</b><indent=40px>\n<b>Ctrl+S to Save:</b> You can now quickly save the current project with Ctrl+S.\n<b>Auto-Save:</b> New option to automatically save your project. When enabled in Main Options, Sound Show will save the project ~10 seconds after changes, once editing has paused.\n<b>Save Backups:</b> New backup system that keeps previous versions of your project. By default, 1 previous version is kept (configurable in Main Options). Backups use a <i>-prev</i> suffix, for example: <i>projectName-prev.ssp</i>.\n<b>Overwrite Warning:</b> If you try to create a new project using a name that already exists, Sound Show will now warn you before overwriting it.</indent></indent>\n\n<indent=20px><b>Keyboard Shortcuts</b><indent=40px>\n<b>Category navigation:</b> You can now navigate and select categories (tabs) using keyboard mappings (configuration in Options -> Keyboard).\n<b>Hold to change volume:</b> Holding the <i>+</i> or <i>-</i> keys now continuously increases or decreases volume instead of requiring repeated taps.</indent></indent>\n\n<indent=20px><b>Options Management</b><indent=40px>\n<b>Export / Import Settings:</b> You can now export your options to a .sso (Sound Show Options) file and import them later, on the same machine or another machine. These actions are available at the bottom of the Main Options popup.\n<b>Restore Defaults (Fixed):</b> “Restore default values” now correctly resets all options to their factory defaults.</indent></indent>\n\n<indent=20px><b>Help Category</b><indent=40px>\n<b>New Help category:</b> Added a new Help category (question mark icon) next to Search in the Special Category panel. Goal: make the first steps smoother for new users.\n<b>Quick links include:</b>\nGetting started guide\nYouTube channel\nArticles / documentation\n<b>Behavior:</b> Clicking a button opens the link in your web browser.\n<b>Pro option:</b> For Pro users, the Help button can be hidden in the Special Category panel settings.</indent></indent>\n\n<indent=20px><b>Volume Normalization</b><indent=40px>\n<b>Per-Sound Normalized Volume:</b> Each sound now has a new <i>Normalized Volume</i> field in its configuration popup. This is an internal multiplier that affects how loud the sound actually plays. This is now the recommended setting to use if a sound is too loud or too quiet. The existing <i>Volume</i> setting is still available to define the starting volume for playback, which is useful when you want a specific start level, not global loudness correction.\n<b>Category-wide Normalize Action:</b> In a category’s configuration popup, there’s a new <i>Normalize</i> action. It analyzes all sounds in that category and adjusts their normalized volume so they play at a more consistent level.</indent></indent>", "link_url": "https://soundshow.app/downloads", "link_label": "Download the new version", "image": "", "create_date": "2025-10-26 00:26:07", "message_date": "2025-10-25", "message_type": "update"}]}
